-- title:
--   Standard domain $\mathcal E_U$
-- statement:
--   For a set $U\subseteq M$, the **standard domain** $\mathcal E_U$ is the closure in $\mathcal E$ of
--   $$\mathrm{span}\{e^{i\Phi(g)}:\ g\in C_c^\infty(M,\mathbb R),\ \operatorname{supp} g\subseteq U\}.$$
--
--   **Formalization Note** The paper's Definition 1.2 takes $f\in H_{-1}(M)$ with $\operatorname{supp}f\subset\Omega$; the closed span is generated by smooth compactly supported functions, as in the proof of Theorem 4.4 ("smooth test functions with compact, positive-time support") (Reading 5).
-- source:
--   Jaffe, Ritter, Quantum Field Theory on Curved Backgrounds. I. The Euclidean Functional Integral, arXiv:hep-th/0609003v1, Definition 1.2, p. 5

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_JRCurvedQFT_SharpTime_expVec
import Definitions.Def_JRCurvedQFT_SharpTime_ofFunction
import Definitions.Def_JRCurvedQFT_SharpTime_IsTestFunction

open scoped Manifold ContDiff ENNReal Topology
open Bundle MeasureTheory

namespace JRCurvedQFT.SharpTime

variable {d : ℕ} {M : Type} [EMetricSpace M]
  [ChartedSpace (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) M] [IsManifold 𝓘(ℝ, EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) ∞ M]
  [RiemannianBundle (fun (x : M) ↦ TangentSpace 𝓘(ℝ, EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) x)]

/-- The **standard domain** `ℰ_U`: the closed span in `ℰ` of the vectors `e^{iΦ(g)}`, `g` a test
function with support in `U`.

Jaffe, Ritter, *Quantum Field Theory on Curved Backgrounds. I. The Euclidean Functional Integral*, arXiv:hep-th/0609003v1, Definition 1.2, p. 5: "For an open set Ω ⊆ M, the standard domain in ℰ corresponding to Ω
is: E_Ω = span{e^{iΦ(f)} : f ∈ H₋₁(M), supp(f) ⊂ Ω}. Let ℰ_Ω denote the closure in ℰ of E_Ω."

**Formalization Note** Reading 5: the generating `f` are real `C_c^∞(M)` functions with
`tsupport f ⊆ U`, as in the proof of Theorem 4.4 (p. 25: "smooth test functions {g_n} with
compact, positive-time support"). -/
noncomputable def standardDomain [MeasurableSpace M] (μ : Measure M) {Ω : Type}
    [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) [IsFiniteMeasure P] (Φ : ((M → ℝ) → ℝ) → Ω → ℝ)
    (U : Set M) : Submodule ℂ (Lp ℂ 2 P) :=
  (Submodule.span ℂ {A | ∃ g : M → ℝ, IsTestFunction (d := d) g ∧ tsupport g ⊆ U ∧
    A = expVec P Φ (ofFunction μ g)}).topologicalClosure

end JRCurvedQFT.SharpTime


